                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 30 at 1:06AM MST until August 31 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "description": "The first round of rainfall is wrapping up with only isolated\nshowers or weak storms possible for the rest of tonight through\nSunday morning. Another round of showers and storms are expected for\nSunday evening. Heavy rainfall and localized flooding will be\npossible Sunday evening into early Sunday night, particularly across\nMaricopa and Pinal Counties.\n\nThe Flood Watch is cancelled for a portion of south central Arizona,\nincluding the following areas, Aguila Valley, Buckeye/Avondale, Cave\nCreek/New River, Central Phoenix, Deer Valley, East Valley, Fountain\nHills/East Mesa, Mazatzal Mountains, New River Mesa, North\nPhoenix/Glendale, Northwest Valley, Rio Verde/Salt River,\nScottsdale/Paradise Valley, South Mountain/Ahwatukee, Southeast\nValley/Queen Creek, Tonopah Desert and Tonto Basin.\n\nFlooding is no longer expected to pose a threat tonight, but another\nround of storms with heavy rainfall is expected Sunday evening.\nPlease continue to heed remaining road closures.",
