                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 30 at 1:06AM MST until August 31 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "description": "The first round of rainfall is wrapping up with only isolated\nshowers or weak storms possible for the rest of tonight through\nSunday morning. Another round of showers and storms are expected for\nSunday evening. Heavy rainfall and localized flooding will be\npossible Sunday evening into early Sunday night, particularly across\nMaricopa and Pinal Counties.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of south central Arizona, including the following\nareas, Apache Junction/Gold Canyon, Dripping Springs, Globe/Miami,\nNorthwest Pinal County, Pinal/Superstition Mountains, San Carlos,\nSonoran Desert Natl Monument, Southeast Gila County, Superior and\nWest Pinal County.\n\n* WHEN...From this evening through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ample moisture and atmospheric instability will again combine\nwith a weather system positioned over western portions of the\nregion to promote scattered thunderstorms capable of producing\nheavy rainfall from Sunday evening into Sunday night. Training of\nstorms could result in localized rainfall amounts of over two\ninches within the watch area.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
